# Engineering Governance

Behavior-changing engineering work must be traceable to an approved product decision and an OpenSpec change.

Treat approved specifications as behavioral contracts.

Product owns WHY and WHAT.

Engineering owns HOW.

Do not silently expand approved scope.

Do not silently change product requirements during implementation.

Surface specification ambiguity instead of inventing product intent.

Run relevant tests before considering implementation complete.

The agent that implements a change must not be the sole authority that approves it.

Use independent verification for significant behavior-changing work.

Implementation completion does not equal product approval.